<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Chandor</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Chandrapura</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Chandor is a village in the Salcete area of South <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/goa">Goa</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, which as Chandrapura was an early capital of the Kadambas of Goa from the 10th century, and earlier of local rulers. Excavations have found the remains of an early temple there. The village is now known for its grand Portuguese-era houses.</p></div>
